<bx:include template="partials/_head.bxm">
<bx:output>
<section class="bx-hero">
  <h1>BoxLang Express</h1>
  <p class="bx-tagline">An Express.js-style API for building lightweight HTTP servers in BoxLang — routing, middleware, sessions, views, and file uploads, on top of the JDK's own <code class="bx-inline">com.sun.net.httpserver.HttpServer</code>.</p>
  <div class="bx-hero-actions">
    <a class="bx-btn bx-btn-primary" href="/docs/getting-started">Get Started</a>
    <a class="bx-btn bx-btn-secondary" href="/docs/routing">Read the Docs</a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bx-home-section">
<pre class="bx-code"><span class="bx-code-label">bxs</span><code>app = boxExpress()

app.use( boxExpressJSON() )

app.get( "/", ( req, res ) => {
    res.send( "Hello from BoxLang Express!" )
} )

app.get( "/users/:id", ( req, res ) => {
    res.json( { id: req.params.id } )
} )

app.listen( 3000, ( port ) => {
    println( "Listening on ##port##" )
} )</code></pre>
</section>

<section class="bx-home-section">
  <p class="bx-section-title">Why BoxLang Express</p>
  <div class="bx-feature-grid">
    <div class="bx-feature-card">
      <h3>Familiar routing</h3>
      <p><code class="bx-inline">app.get/post/put/patch/delete</code>, route params, wildcards, and mountable sub-routers — the same shape as Express.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bx-feature-card">
      <h3>Middleware stack</h3>
      <p><code class="bx-inline">app.use()</code> with the standard <code class="bx-inline">(req, res, next)</code> signature, plus 4-arg error middleware.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bx-feature-card">
      <h3>Sessions, views, uploads</h3>
      <p>Cookie-based sessions, <code class="bx-inline">.bxm</code>/<code class="bx-inline">.hbs</code> view rendering, and multipart file uploads out of the box.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bx-feature-card">
      <h3>Virtual-thread concurrency</h3>
      <p>Every request runs on its own JDK virtual thread — no manual thread-pool tuning, no request serialization.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bx-feature-card">
      <h3>Dev-mode auto-reload</h3>
      <p><code class="bx-inline">app.set("reloadOnChange", true)</code> watches your source and restarts the process on save.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bx-feature-card">
      <h3>Clean process lifecycle</h3>
      <p>Ctrl-C/SIGTERM shut the server down gracefully; a port already in use exits with a message, not a stack trace.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bx-home-section">
  <p class="bx-section-title">Documentation</p>
  <figure class="bx-screenshot">
    <a href="/docs/getting-started"><img src="/assets/img/screenshots/docs-preview.png" alt="The BoxLang Express documentation, showing the sidebar navigation and a docs page"></a>
    <figcaption>The docs site itself — sidebar nav, code blocks, and callouts, all built with plain .bxm partials.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <div class="bx-doc-links">
    <a class="bx-doc-link" href="/docs/getting-started">
